*Impacts of Common Pollutants [1]:* Common pollutants from emission hazards cause harmful effects on human health and the environment, leading to respiratory diseases, cardiovascular problems, reduced lung function, nervous system damage, and premature deaths, while contributing to air pollution, smog formation, and climate change.

