+ *Emission Hazard:* Fossil fuel/biomass burning releases $"CO"$, $"CO"_2$, $"    "_x$, $"SO"_x$, hydrocarbons, and PM, causing smog, respiratory diseases, global warming, and acid rain.
+ *Battery Hazard:* Toxic materials (lead, mercury, cadmium, acid) cause soil/water pollution, enter the food chain, and increase e-waste.
+ *Nuclear Hazard:* Radioactive materials cause cell damage, cancer, genetic defects, and environmental contamination.

*Q. How does nuclear fusion occur and how is it applied to generate electricity? How are nuclear plants secured from emission hazards? [1+3]*
+ *Nuclear Fusion Process [1]:* Two light atomic nuclei (e.g., deuterium and tritium) combine under extreme temperature and pressure to form a heavier nucleus (helium), releasing a large amount of heat.
+ *Electricity Application [3]:* Fusion heat #sym.arrow produces steam #sym.arrow drives a turbine #sym.arrow generator converts mechanical energy into electricity.
+ *Securing Plants [3]:* Use strong concrete-steel containment structures, thick radiation shielding (concrete, lead, water), strict radioactive waste management, and continuous monitoring/emergency cooling systems.

*Q. Discuss the status of emission hazard in context of Nepal. [3]*
+ *Vehicle Emissions:* Rapid vehicle growth and poor vehicle maintenance in urban centers (like Kathmandu Valley) increase $"CO"$, $"HC"$, $"NO"_x$, and PM levels.
+ *Household Air Pollution:* Heavy reliance on biomass fuels (firewood, dung, agricultural residues) with poor indoor ventilation severely impacts women and children.
+ *Industrial/Construction Emissions:* Brick kilns, factories, and construction dust degrade local air quality.
+ *Health & Environmental Effects:* Triggers respiratory and heart diseases, climate change, and smog formation.